  "notes": "No previous similar events reported (narrative states 'None'), so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER node emitted. Two distinct open-valve discoveries (Breathing Air penetration valves, then Instrument Air penetration valve found during extent-of-condition) modeled as parallel FailureMode nodes both leading to the same consequence. Check valve outside containment in the BA flowpath is explicitly stated to have mitigated potential release and is modeled as a backup via BACKED_UP_BY from the consequence, though it is a Component rather than a System backup. IA penetration's inside valve remained operable (closed) throughout, so that penetration's isolation function was preserved via inside valve position, but only the outside manual valve failure is modeled as the FailureMode per narrative wording."
